// Weather Ahead — local signing settings
//
// Copy this file to `Config/Local.xcconfig` (which is gitignored) and fill in
// your own values. Xcode reads it automatically as the project's base
// configuration, so you never have to edit the project file.
//
//     cp Config/Local.xcconfig.example Config/Local.xcconfig
//
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM
//   Your 10-character Apple Developer Team ID. Find it at
//   https://developer.apple.com/account under Membership details, or in
//   Xcode → Settings → Accounts.
//
// PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER
//   Must be a bundle id *you* own, because WeatherKit is authorised per App ID.
//   Register it at https://developer.apple.com/account/resources/identifiers
//   and tick the WeatherKit capability, then enable WeatherKit for the same
//   App ID in App Store Connect. Allow up to ~30 minutes for it to activate.
//
// Without a WeatherKit-enabled App ID the app still builds and runs — the
// timeline, places and permissions all work — but every row will show
// "No weather data".

DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =
PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER = com.example.weatherahead
